{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/03-turn-construction-recovery-cascade.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/03-turn-construction-recovery-cascade/003-implementor.json\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/recovery.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial Story 3 verification against the story ACs/TCs, tech-design DD-4/DD-7, test-plan Flow 3, production turn compose/derive/recovery paths, logging surface, work-queue live-work semantics, and Story 3 tests. Configured story and epic gates passed, but a focused recovery race probe failed and required TC coverage is missing.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Recovery write-back can clobber a worker's ready result\",\"evidence\":\"TC-3.8d requires a live worker to win after floor rendering. In packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/recovery.ts:67-83, recoverDerivation updates any row matching subject/type/source_version after the live-work check; it does not guard against the row already being ready. A focused probe seeded a ready row with content \\\"real result\\\", called recoverDerivation with \\\"floor result\\\", and failed with: \\\"expected ready worker content to survive, got floor result\\\". This models the race where a claimed worker completes and deletes its work_item just before recovery opens its transaction. The Story 3 test at packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts:255-293 only proves a queued live item remains untouched; it never completes the worker and asserts the real ready result survives.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/recovery.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8d\",\"DD-4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-03-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Required cascade TC scenarios are not covered in story tests\",\"evidence\":\"The story/test-plan map TC-3.2c, TC-3.4a, and TC-3.5a to packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts. That file currently has six tests at lines 82, 107, 140, 172, 224, and 255, covering ready use, pending floor, failed floor, re-derive, tool truncation, and queued live-work deferral. rg found no test evidence for TC-3.2c, TC-3.4a, TC-3.5a, floor-unavailable/original fallback, runtime-change placement during turn construction, or multiple not-ready derivations producing a no-hole turn.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"AC-3.4\",\"TC-3.4a\",\"AC-3.5\",\"TC-3.5a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Recovery write-back can clobber a worker's ready result\",\"evidence\":\"TC-3.8d requires a live worker to win after floor rendering. In packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/recovery.ts:67-83, recoverDerivation updates any row matching subject/type/source_version after the live-work check; it does not guard against the row already being ready. A focused probe seeded a ready row with content \\\"real result\\\", called recoverDerivation with \\\"floor result\\\", and failed with: \\\"expected ready worker content to survive, got floor result\\\". This models the race where a claimed worker completes and deletes its work_item just before recovery opens its transaction. The Story 3 test at packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts:255-293 only proves a queued live item remains untouched; it never completes the worker and asserts the real ready result survives.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/recovery.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8d\",\"DD-4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-03-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Required cascade TC scenarios are not covered in story tests\",\"evidence\":\"The story/test-plan map TC-3.2c, TC-3.4a, and TC-3.5a to packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts. That file currently has six tests at lines 82, 107, 140, 172, 224, and 255, covering ready use, pending floor, failed floor, re-derive, tool truncation, and queued live-work deferral. rg found no test evidence for TC-3.2c, TC-3.4a, TC-3.5a, floor-unavailable/original fallback, runtime-change placement during turn construction, or multiple not-ready derivations producing a no-hole turn.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/turn-cascade.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"AC-3.4\",\"TC-3.4a\",\"AC-3.5\",\"TC-3.5a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1 / TC-3.1a\",\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2a\",\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2b\",\"AC-3.3 / TC-3.3a\",\"AC-3.6 / TC-3.6a\",\"AC-3.6 / TC-3.6b\",\"AC-3.7 / TC-3.7a\",\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8a\",\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8b\",\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8c\",\"Story gate passed\",\"Epic gate passed\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2c\",\"AC-3.4 / TC-3.4a\",\"AC-3.5 / TC-3.5a\",\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8d\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"cd pack